{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Forms often edit data loaded from an API. A server-state library such as\nTanStack Query should own fetching, caching, loading, and retries; TanStack Form\nshould own the editable copy."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"There are two supported ways to provide async initial values: wait to create the\nform until the data is ready, or create it immediately with complete fallback\nvalues. Choose the approach that best matches the loading experience your UI\nneeds."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"wait-for-data-before-creating-the-editor","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Wait for data before creating the editor"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Render a loading or error state first, then mount a component whose\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"defaultValues"},{"type":"text","value":" are complete."}]},{"type":"code","value":"<!-- UserPage.svelte -->\n<script lang=\"ts\">\n  import { createQuery } from '@tanstack/svelte-query'\n  import { derived, toStore } from 'svelte/store'\n  import UserEditor from './UserEditor.svelte'\n  import type { User } from './types.js'\n\n  const { userId }: { userId: string } = $props()\n  const userIdStore = toStore(() => userId)\n  const userQuery = createQuery(\n    derived(userIdStore, (currentUserId) => ({\n      queryKey: ['user', currentUserId],\n      queryFn: async (): Promise<User> => {\n        const response = await fetch(`/api/users/${currentUserId}`)\n        return response.json()\n      },\n    })),\n  )\n</script>\n\n{#if $userQuery.isPending}\n  <p>Loading…</p>\n{:else if $userQuery.isError}\n  <p role=\"alert\">Could not load the user.</p>\n{:else}\n  {#key userId}\n    <UserEditor user={$userQuery.data} />\n  {/key}\n{/if}","lang":"svelte"},{"type":"code","value":"<!-- UserEditor.svelte -->\n<script lang=\"ts\">\n  import { createForm } from '@tanstack/svelte-form'\n  import type { User } from './types.js'\n\n  const { user }: { user: User } = $props()\n  const form = createForm(() => ({\n    defaultValues: user,\n    onSubmit: async ({ value }) => {\n      await fetch('/api/users', {\n        method: 'PUT',\n        headers: { 'content-type': 'application/json' },\n        body: JSON.stringify(value),\n      })\n    },\n  }))\n</script>\n\n<form\n  onsubmit={(event) => {\n    event.preventDefault()\n    form.handleSubmit()\n  }}\n>\n  <!-- fields -->\n</form>","lang":"svelte"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This pattern is useful when no form state is needed during loading. Mounting the\neditor only after data exists also makes it explicit when switching records\nshould create a fresh form. The keyed block recreates the editor when "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"userId"},{"type":"text","value":"\nchanges."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"create-the-form-before-data-arrives","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Create the form before data arrives"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"You can instead call "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createForm"},{"type":"text","value":" in the same component as "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createQuery"},{"type":"text","value":".\nProvide a static, shape-complete fallback so "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"defaultValues"},{"type":"text","value":" are never\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"undefined"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"code","value":"<script lang=\"ts\">\n  import { createForm } from '@tanstack/svelte-form'\n  import { createQuery } from '@tanstack/svelte-query'\n  import { derived, toStore } from 'svelte/store'\n  import type { User } from './types.js'\n\n  const { userId }: { userId: string } = $props()\n  const emptyUser: User = {\n    firstName: '',\n    lastName: '',\n  }\n\n  const userIdStore = toStore(() => userId)\n  const userQuery = createQuery(\n    derived(userIdStore, (currentUserId) => ({\n      queryKey: ['user', currentUserId],\n      queryFn: async (): Promise<User> => {\n        const response = await fetch(`/api/users/${currentUserId}`)\n        return response.json()\n      },\n    })),\n  )\n\n  const form = createForm(() => ({\n    defaultValues: $userQuery.data ?? emptyUser,\n    onSubmit: async ({ value }) => {\n      await fetch('/api/users', {\n        method: 'PUT',\n        headers: { 'content-type': 'application/json' },\n        body: JSON.stringify(value),\n      })\n    },\n  }))\n</script>\n\n{#if $userQuery.isPending}\n  <p>Loading…</p>\n{:else if $userQuery.isError}\n  <p role=\"alert\">Could not load the user.</p>\n{:else}\n  <form\n    onsubmit={(event) => {\n      event.preventDefault()\n      form.handleSubmit()\n    }}\n  >\n    <!-- fields -->\n  </form>\n{/if}","lang":"svelte"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Because "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createForm"},{"type":"text","value":" receives an options function, reading "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"$userQuery"},{"type":"text","value":" inside\nthat function keeps the options reactive. When the query data replaces the\nfallback, TanStack Form applies the new "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"defaultValues"},{"type":"text","value":" to untouched fields\nwhile preserving fields the user has already touched."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This is the approach demonstrated by the repository's\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"examples/svelte/query-integration"},{"type":"text","value":" example."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"background-refetches-and-record-changes","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Background refetches and record changes"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"defaultValues"},{"type":"text","value":" establish the form's baseline; they are not a fully controlled\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"values"},{"type":"text","value":" prop. In the fallback pattern, later "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"defaultValues"},{"type":"text","value":" updates use the\nsame touched-field-preserving behavior."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If background refetches arrive while a user is editing, decide at the product\nlevel whether to keep local edits, prompt before replacing them, or call\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"form.reset(nextValues)"},{"type":"text","value":" deliberately. Do not overwrite in-progress input merely\nbecause a query refreshed."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"When switching to a different record, either recreate a keyed editor as in the\nfirst pattern or deliberately reset the existing form. Otherwise, touched\nvalues from the previous record can be preserved when the new defaults arrive."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"wait-for-data-before-creating-the-editor","text":"Wait for data before creating the editor","level":2},{"id":"create-the-form-before-data-arrives","text":"Create the form before data arrives","level":2},{"id":"background-refetches-and-record-changes","text":"Background refetches and record changes","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nForms often edit data loaded from an API. A server-state library such as\nTanStack Query should own fetching, caching, loading, and retries; TanStack Form\nshould own the editable copy.\n\nThere are two supported ways to provide async initial values: wait to create the\nform until the data is ready, or create it immediately with complete fallback\nvalues. Choose the approach that best matches the loading experience your UI\nneeds.\n\n## Wait for data before creating the editor\n\nRender a loading or error state first, then mount a component whose\n`defaultValues` are complete.\n\n```svelte\n<!-- UserPage.svelte -->\n<script lang=\"ts\">\n  import { createQuery } from '@tanstack/svelte-query'\n  import { derived, toStore } from 'svelte/store'\n  import UserEditor from './UserEditor.svelte'\n  import type { User } from './types.js'\n\n  const { userId }: { userId: string } = $props()\n  const userIdStore = toStore(() => userId)\n  const userQuery = createQuery(\n    derived(userIdStore, (currentUserId) => ({\n      queryKey: ['user', currentUserId],\n      queryFn: async (): Promise<User> => {\n        const response = await fetch(`/api/users/${currentUserId}`)\n        return response.json()\n      },\n    })),\n  )\n</script>\n\n{#if $userQuery.isPending}\n  <p>Loading…</p>\n{:else if $userQuery.isError}\n  <p role=\"alert\">Could not load the user.</p>\n{:else}\n  {#key userId}\n    <UserEditor user={$userQuery.data} />\n  {/key}\n{/if}\n```\n\n```svelte\n<!-- UserEditor.svelte -->\n<script lang=\"ts\">\n  import { createForm } from '@tanstack/svelte-form'\n  import type { User } from './types.js'\n\n  const { user }: { user: User } = $props()\n  const form = createForm(() => ({\n    defaultValues: user,\n    onSubmit: async ({ value }) => {\n      await fetch('/api/users', {\n        method: 'PUT',\n        headers: { 'content-type': 'application/json' },\n        body: JSON.stringify(value),\n      })\n    },\n  }))\n</script>\n\n<form\n  onsubmit={(event) => {\n    event.preventDefault()\n    form.handleSubmit()\n  }}\n>\n  <!-- fields -->\n</form>\n```\n\nThis pattern is useful when no form state is needed during loading. Mounting the\neditor only after data exists also makes it explicit when switching records\nshould create a fresh form. The keyed block recreates the editor when `userId`\nchanges.\n\n## Create the form before data arrives\n\nYou can instead call `createForm` in the same component as `createQuery`.\nProvide a static, shape-complete fallback so `defaultValues` are never\n`undefined`.\n\n```svelte\n<script lang=\"ts\">\n  import { createForm } from '@tanstack/svelte-form'\n  import { createQuery } from '@tanstack/svelte-query'\n  import { derived, toStore } from 'svelte/store'\n  import type { User } from './types.js'\n\n  const { userId }: { userId: string } = $props()\n  const emptyUser: User = {\n    firstName: '',\n    lastName: '',\n  }\n\n  const userIdStore = toStore(() => userId)\n  const userQuery = createQuery(\n    derived(userIdStore, (currentUserId) => ({\n      queryKey: ['user', currentUserId],\n      queryFn: async (): Promise<User> => {\n        const response = await fetch(`/api/users/${currentUserId}`)\n        return response.json()\n      },\n    })),\n  )\n\n  const form = createForm(() => ({\n    defaultValues: $userQuery.data ?? emptyUser,\n    onSubmit: async ({ value }) => {\n      await fetch('/api/users', {\n        method: 'PUT',\n        headers: { 'content-type': 'application/json' },\n        body: JSON.stringify(value),\n      })\n    },\n  }))\n</script>\n\n{#if $userQuery.isPending}\n  <p>Loading…</p>\n{:else if $userQuery.isError}\n  <p role=\"alert\">Could not load the user.</p>\n{:else}\n  <form\n    onsubmit={(event) => {\n      event.preventDefault()\n      form.handleSubmit()\n    }}\n  >\n    <!-- fields -->\n  </form>\n{/if}\n```\n\nBecause `createForm` receives an options function, reading `$userQuery` inside\nthat function keeps the options reactive. When the query data replaces the\nfallback, TanStack Form applies the new `defaultValues` to untouched fields\nwhile preserving fields the user has already touched.\n\nThis is the approach demonstrated by the repository's\n`examples/svelte/query-integration` example.\n\n## Background refetches and record changes\n\n`defaultValues` establish the form's baseline; they are not a fully controlled\n`values` prop. In the fallback pattern, later `defaultValues` updates use the\nsame touched-field-preserving behavior.\n\nIf background refetches arrive while a user is editing, decide at the product\nlevel whether to keep local edits, prompt before replacing them, or call\n`form.reset(nextValues)` deliberately. Do not overwrite in-progress input merely\nbecause a query refreshed.\n\nWhen switching to a different record, either recreate a keyed editor as in the\nfirst pattern or deliberately reset the existing form. Otherwise, touched\nvalues from the previous record can be preserved when the new defaults arrive.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: async-initial-values\ntitle: Async Initial Values\n---\n\nForms often edit data loaded from an API. A server-state library such as\nTanStack Query should own fetching, caching, loading, and retries; TanStack Form\nshould own the editable copy.\n\nThere are two supported ways to provide async initial values: wait to create the\nform until the data is ready, or create it immediately with complete fallback\nvalues. Choose the approach that best matches the loading experience your UI\nneeds.\n\n## Wait for data before creating the editor\n\nRender a loading or error state first, then mount a component whose\n`defaultValues` are complete.\n\n```svelte\n<!-- UserPage.svelte -->\n<script lang=\"ts\">\n  import { createQuery } from '@tanstack/svelte-query'\n  import { derived, toStore } from 'svelte/store'\n  import UserEditor from './UserEditor.svelte'\n  import type { User } from './types.js'\n\n  const { userId }: { userId: string } = $props()\n  const userIdStore = toStore(() => userId)\n  const userQuery = createQuery(\n    derived(userIdStore, (currentUserId) => ({\n      queryKey: ['user', currentUserId],\n      queryFn: async (): Promise<User> => {\n        const response = await fetch(`/api/users/${currentUserId}`)\n        return response.json()\n      },\n    })),\n  )\n</script>\n\n{#if $userQuery.isPending}\n  <p>Loading…</p>\n{:else if $userQuery.isError}\n  <p role=\"alert\">Could not load the user.</p>\n{:else}\n  {#key userId}\n    <UserEditor user={$userQuery.data} />\n  {/key}\n{/if}\n```\n\n```svelte\n<!-- UserEditor.svelte -->\n<script lang=\"ts\">\n  import { createForm } from '@tanstack/svelte-form'\n  import type { User } from './types.js'\n\n  const { user }: { user: User } = $props()\n  const form = createForm(() => ({\n    defaultValues: user,\n    onSubmit: async ({ value }) => {\n      await fetch('/api/users', {\n        method: 'PUT',\n        headers: { 'content-type': 'application/json' },\n        body: JSON.stringify(value),\n      })\n    },\n  }))\n</script>\n\n<form\n  onsubmit={(event) => {\n    event.preventDefault()\n    form.handleSubmit()\n  }}\n>\n  <!-- fields -->\n</form>\n```\n\nThis pattern is useful when no form state is needed during loading. Mounting the\neditor only after data exists also makes it explicit when switching records\nshould create a fresh form. The keyed block recreates the editor when `userId`\nchanges.\n\n## Create the form before data arrives\n\nYou can instead call `createForm` in the same component as `createQuery`.\nProvide a static, shape-complete fallback so `defaultValues` are never\n`undefined`.\n\n```svelte\n<script lang=\"ts\">\n  import { createForm } from '@tanstack/svelte-form'\n  import { createQuery } from '@tanstack/svelte-query'\n  import { derived, toStore } from 'svelte/store'\n  import type { User } from './types.js'\n\n  const { userId }: { userId: string } = $props()\n  const emptyUser: User = {\n    firstName: '',\n    lastName: '',\n  }\n\n  const userIdStore = toStore(() => userId)\n  const userQuery = createQuery(\n    derived(userIdStore, (currentUserId) => ({\n      queryKey: ['user', currentUserId],\n      queryFn: async (): Promise<User> => {\n        const response = await fetch(`/api/users/${currentUserId}`)\n        return response.json()\n      },\n    })),\n  )\n\n  const form = createForm(() => ({\n    defaultValues: $userQuery.data ?? emptyUser,\n    onSubmit: async ({ value }) => {\n      await fetch('/api/users', {\n        method: 'PUT',\n        headers: { 'content-type': 'application/json' },\n        body: JSON.stringify(value),\n      })\n    },\n  }))\n</script>\n\n{#if $userQuery.isPending}\n  <p>Loading…</p>\n{:else if $userQuery.isError}\n  <p role=\"alert\">Could not load the user.</p>\n{:else}\n  <form\n    onsubmit={(event) => {\n      event.preventDefault()\n      form.handleSubmit()\n    }}\n  >\n    <!-- fields -->\n  </form>\n{/if}\n```\n\nBecause `createForm` receives an options function, reading `$userQuery` inside\nthat function keeps the options reactive. When the query data replaces the\nfallback, TanStack Form applies the new `defaultValues` to untouched fields\nwhile preserving fields the user has already touched.\n\nThis is the approach demonstrated by the repository's\n`examples/svelte/query-integration` example.\n\n## Background refetches and record changes\n\n`defaultValues` establish the form's baseline; they are not a fully controlled\n`values` prop. In the fallback pattern, later `defaultValues` updates use the\nsame touched-field-preserving behavior.\n\nIf background refetches arrive while a user is editing, decide at the product\nlevel whether to keep local edits, prompt before replacing them, or call\n`form.reset(nextValues)` deliberately. Do not overwrite in-progress input merely\nbecause a query refreshed.\n\nWhen switching to a different record, either recreate a keyed editor as in the\nfirst pattern or deliberately reset the existing form. Otherwise, touched\nvalues from the previous record can be preserved when the new defaults arrive.\n"}
